{
  "title": "Continuous profiles: Core, Minion, nl6",
  "uid": "onms-profiles-services",
  "description": "Audience: engineer. Where do OpenNMS Core, Minion and the nl6 simulator spend CPU and memory during a benchmark run, and are their profiles arriving? Feeds the decision of which code path to tune next and whether profiler overhead is acceptable for the run. Source: Grafana Pyroscope on the monitoring host (push from the pyroscope-java agent and nl6's built-in profiler) plus Pyroscope's own metrics in Prometheus.",
  "tags": [
    "opennms",
    "pyroscope",
    "profiling",
    "entity-detail",
    "audience:engineer"
  ],
  "timezone": "utc",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "links": [
    {
      "type": "link",
      "title": "Profiles Drilldown",
      "icon": "external link",
      "url": "/a/grafana-pyroscope-app/explore?explorationType=flame-graph&var-dataSource=${datasource}&var-profileMetricId=${profile_type}&${__url_time_range}",
      "keepTime": true,
      "includeVars": false,
      "targetBlank": false,
      "tooltip": "Grafana's profile explorer for the selected service and profile type"
    },
    {
      "type": "link",
      "title": "Core internals (Prometheus)",
      "icon": "dashboard",
      "url": "/d/42118f3c-3c63-451a-9692-c3dd43b854c0",
      "keepTime": true,
      "includeVars": false,
      "targetBlank": false,
      "tooltip": "JVM and OpenNMS metrics for the same window"
    },
    {
      "type": "link",
      "title": "Minion Kafka IPC",
      "icon": "dashboard",
      "url": "/d/onms-minion-internal",
      "keepTime": true,
      "includeVars": false,
      "targetBlank": false,
      "tooltip": "RPC path between Core and Minions"
    }
  ],
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "label": "Profiles data source",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "grafana-pyroscope-datasource",
        "current": {},
        "hide": 0,
        "refresh": 1,
        "description": "The Pyroscope server. One is provisioned per lab (uid pyroscope)."
      },
      {
        "name": "prometheus",
        "label": "Metrics data source",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {},
        "hide": 0,
        "refresh": 1,
        "description": "Prometheus that scrapes the Pyroscope server's own /metrics (job pyroscope)."
      },
      {
        "name": "service",
        "label": "Service",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "grafana-pyroscope-datasource",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "query": {
          "refId": "PyroscopeVariableQuery",
          "type": "labelValue",
          "profileTypeId": "process_cpu:cpu:nanoseconds:cpu:nanoseconds",
          "labelName": "service_name"
        },
        "definition": "service_name values with a CPU profile",
        "multi": true,
        "includeAll": true,
        "allValue": ".*",
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1,
        "current": {
          "selected": true,
          "text": [
            "All"
          ],
          "value": [
            "$__all"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Services pushing profiles: OpenNMS Core and Minion under the application name their agents send, nl6, and the Pyroscope server's own self-profile, which doubles as proof that the pipeline works."
      },
      {
        "name": "profile_type",
        "label": "Profile type",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "grafana-pyroscope-datasource",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "query": {
          "refId": "PyroscopeVariableQuery",
          "type": "profileType"
        },
        "definition": "profile types present on the server",
        "multi": false,
        "includeAll": false,
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1,
        "current": {
          "selected": true,
          "text": "process_cpu:cpu:nanoseconds:cpu:nanoseconds",
          "value": "process_cpu:cpu:nanoseconds:cpu:nanoseconds"
        },
        "description": "Which sample to look at. CPU is common to Java and Go. Allocation and lock types differ: Java uses memory:alloc_in_new_tlab_* and mutex:*, Go uses memory:alloc_*, memory:inuse_*, goroutines and block:*."
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Verdict: are profiles arriving, and how hot are the services?",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Profiles received by the server, last 5 min",
      "description": "Count of profile uploads the Pyroscope distributor accepted in the last five minutes, all services combined (pyroscope_distributor_profiles_received_total, scraped by Prometheus). Normal: steadily above zero once at least one agent pushes; Pyroscope's own self-profile alone contributes roughly one upload per 15 s. Zero means nothing is arriving: check the agent's PYROSCOPE_SERVER_ADDRESS (Core, Minion) or the -profiling-pyroscope flag (nl6), and the server's /ready. This number does not split by service; the panels to the right and below do.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${prometheus}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${prometheus}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(pyroscope_distributor_profiles_received_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "profiles received"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "value": null,
                "color": "#D9414B"
              },
              {
                "value": 1,
                "color": "#2E9E63"
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "range",
              "options": {
                "from": null,
                "to": 0.99,
                "result": {
                  "text": "none arriving"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "value",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Request error rate at the server",
      "description": "HTTP and Connect requests per second the Pyroscope server answered with a non-2xx or non-3xx status, all routes except the readiness probe (pyroscope_request_duration_seconds_count by status_code). Normal is zero. A steady non-zero value while profiles are pushed means the server is rejecting uploads: check the server log for the status code (413 payload too large, 429 rate limited, 5xx storage) before blaming the agents. Readiness 503s during start-up are excluded.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${prometheus}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${prometheus}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(pyroscope_request_duration_seconds_count{status_code!~\"[23]..\", route!=\"ready\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "failed requests"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "decimals": 2,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "value": null,
                "color": "#2E9E63"
              },
              {
                "value": 0.01,
                "color": "#D9414B"
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "range",
              "options": {
                "from": null,
                "to": 0.009,
                "result": {
                  "text": "none failing"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "value",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Collector saturation: CPU and memory vs container caps",
      "description": "How much of its docker caps the Pyroscope container uses: CPU as a share of the 1.0-core quota (rate of process_cpu_seconds_total) and resident memory as a share of the 1 GiB limit (process_resident_memory_bytes), scraped by Prometheus under job pyroscope. Normal for three services is well under 30% of either. Above 70% the collector, not the system under test, becomes the thing being measured: reduce profile types or sampling rate, or raise pyroscope_cpus / pyroscope_memory in the role defaults. Values are 0 to 1 shares, shown as percent.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${prometheus}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${prometheus}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(process_cpu_seconds_total{job=\"pyroscope\"}[$__rate_interval])) / 1.0",
          "legendFormat": "CPU of 1 core"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${prometheus}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(process_resident_memory_bytes{job=\"pyroscope\"}) / (1024*1024*1024)",
          "legendFormat": "memory of 1 GiB"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 0,
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "value": null,
                "color": "#2E9E63"
              },
              {
                "value": 0.7,
                "color": "#C08215"
              },
              {
                "value": 0.9,
                "color": "#D9414B"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "horizontal"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "CPU consumed right now, per service",
      "description": "CPU cores each selected service is burning, from its CPU profile (process_cpu, sampled at 100 Hz by the Java agent's itimer or Go's runtime profiler, converted to a rate by the data source). Normal during a pm-snmp campaign: Core well below its vCPU count, Minion under one core, nl6 proportional to the fleet size. A service at its vCPU count is CPU-bound: open its flame graph below before tuning thread pools. A service missing here is not pushing profiles.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "grafana-pyroscope-datasource",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "grafana-pyroscope-datasource",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "queryType": "metrics",
          "profileTypeId": "process_cpu:cpu:nanoseconds:cpu:nanoseconds",
          "labelSelector": "{service_name=~\"$service\"}",
          "groupBy": [
            "service_name"
          ],
          "spanSelector": []
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "decimals": 2,
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "value": null,
                "color": "#2E9E63"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byFrameRefID",
              "options": "A"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "displayName",
                "value": "${__field.labels.service_name}"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Profile data arriving at the server, by profile family",
      "description": "Decompressed bytes per second the Pyroscope distributor receives, split by profile family (memory, block, goroutines, cpu and so on), from pyroscope_distributor_received_decompressed_bytes_sum. Use it to see whether a service started or stopped pushing, and what a profiling setting costs in ingest: enabling alloc and lock profiling on the Java agent should show up here as new families. A flat zero while agents are configured points at network or address problems, not at the server.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 15
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${prometheus}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${prometheus}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (type) (rate(pyroscope_distributor_received_decompressed_bytes_sum[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{type}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "Bps",
          "min": 0,
          "decimals": 1,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "off"
            }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "value": null,
                "color": "#2E9E63"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "showLegend": true,
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ],
          "sortBy": "Max",
          "sortDesc": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
